+    "### Using exponential Euler on GPU\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Beyond `jit` and `vmap`, you can sometimes improve performance of `Jaxley` by modifying the solver that is used to solve the differential equations. By default, `Jaxley` uses an implicit (often called \"backward\") Euler solver. In most cases, this solver is accurate and efficient. However, **on GPU**, an exponential Euler solver can sometimes outperform it, especially for smaller morphologies (<1k compartments). To change the solver:\n",
+    "```python\n",
+    "v = jx.integrate(cell, solver=\"exp_euler\")\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
