+    "```python\n",
+    "# You do not have to rerun `customize_solver_exp_euler` until you modify\n",
+    "# length, radius, axial resistivity, or capacitance.\n",
+    "cell.customize_solver_exp_euler(\n",
+    "    exp_euler_transition=cell.build_exp_euler_transition_matrix(delta_t)\n",
+    ")\n",
+    "\n",
+    "v1 = jx.integrate(cell, solver=\"exp_euler\")\n",
+    "cell.set(\"gLeak\", 1e-4)\n",
+    "v2 = jx.integrate(cell, solver=\"exp_euler\")\n",
+    "```\n",
+    "\n",
+    "With these modifications, the exponential Euler can sometimes be five times faster than backward Euler **on GPU**, so it can be worth exploring this. To learn more about solvers, see our [guide on how to choose a solver](https://jaxley.readthedocs.io/en/latest/how_to_guide/choose_solver.html)."
+   ]
